<div xmlns:perseus="http://www.perseus.org/meta/perseus.rdfs#" xmlns:dctype="http://purl.org/dc/dcmitype/" xmlns:tufts="http://www.tufts.edu/" xmlns:alph="http://alpheios.net/namespaces/tei" class="alpheios-lex-text_container en">
    <div class="alpheios-lex-entry" lemma-id="n102871" body-key=""><b><span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">τεκνοποι-έω</span></b> , in 
			Act.
		, of the woman, <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense1"><b>A.</b><i>bear
				children</i>, in 
				Med.
			, of the man, <i>beget them</i>, cf. <i><span class="en">
				X.
				<u>Mem.</u>
				2.2.4
			</span></i> and <i><span class="en">
				5
			</span></i>; 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">μὴ τεκνοποιεῖσθαι ἐξ ἔλλης γυναικός</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					<u>PEleph.</u>
					1.9
				</span></i>
			
			<span class="entity">(iv B.C.)</span> (but <i><span class="en">
				D.S.
			</span></i> reverses this usage, cf. <i><span class="en">
				1.73
			</span></i>, <i><span class="en">
				4.29
			</span></i>); 
				Med.
			, of both parents, <i>breed children</i>, <i><span class="en">
				X.
				<u>Mem.</u>
				4.4.22
			</span></i> sq., <i><span class="en">
				Arist.
				<u>HA</u>
				585b10
			</span></i>; in 
				Med.
			, also, <i>have children begotten for one</i>, <i><span class="en">
				X.
				<u>Lac.</u>
				1.7
			</span></i>, <i><span class="en">
				LXX
				<u>Ge.</u>
				16.2
			</span></i>, <i><span class="en">
				30.3
			</span></i>, <i><span class="en">
				<u>POxy.</u>
				465.154
			</span></i>
			<span class="entity">(ii A.D.)</span>. </div>
        <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense2"><b>II.</b>
			
				Med.
			, of birds, <i><span class="en">
				Arist.
				<u>HA</u>
				597a11
			</span></i>. </div>
        <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense2"><b>III.</b>
			
				Med.
			, <i>adopt</i> a child, <i><span class="en">
				<u>UPZ</u>
				4.5
			</span></i>
			<span class="entity">(ii B.C.)</span>.</div>
